#
# WHY THIS IS PLAINTEXT WHEN forbidden-names.sha256 IS NOT
# The forbidden list is hashed because publishing it would disclose a prospect
# pipeline. This list has the opposite property: every name on it appears in the
# README in plain sight, on purpose. Hashing it would disclose nothing and hide
# the one thing a reviewer needs to check — WHO we claim to have permission from.
#
# An entry is a CARVE-OUT, not a deletion. The name stays in the forbidden list;
# this file allows the specific shingles that brand needs. So consenting
# "Fuhrman" lets the brand appear and still refuses every other real name.
#
# Adding an entry is a claim that someone agreed. Date it and say who.
#
#   date        shingle-sha256                                                    brand / reason
